ublic and private businesses risk, and home business insurance products. This segment also offers coverages for security guards and environmental liability for underground storage tanks, contractors and asbestos, and environmental remediation specialists; and professional liability coverages for errors and omission coverage for small to medium-sized design, technical, computer, and miscellaneous professionals. The company's Property segment offers commercial property insurance, such as fire, wind, difference in conditions, earthquake, flood, and collapse coverages; insurance for office buildings, apartments, condominiums, and industrial and mercantile structures; and cargo, hull, protection and indemnity, marine liability, inland marine, homeowners' and dwelling fire, and other property insurance products. Its Surety segment provides commercial surety bonds for medium and large-sized businesses; small bonds for businesses and individuals; and bonds for small to medium-sized contractors. The company offers reinsurance coverages. It markets its products through branch offices, wholesale and retail brokers, carrier partners, and underwriting and independent agents. RLI Corp. was incorporated in 1965 and is headquartered in Peoria, Illinois.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Craig William Kliethermes CPCU, FCAS, MAAA | President, CEO & Director | Age 60 | Compensation: $6.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $1.6M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers, improving at 8%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $510K of free cash flow annually. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["RLI Corp. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $6.3B market cap on $1.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +3% over the past three years and +9% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 24% against a 7% cost of capital \u2014 a 17-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $609M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 32 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.52\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 95\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield of 3.9% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.039502164502161465},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (11.1% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["38 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"RLI Corp CLO Jeffrey D. Fick Granted 7,500 Stock Options at $67.24 Exercise Price","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/rli-corp-clo-jeffrey-d-fick-granted-7500-stock-options-at-6724-exercise-price","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793744527.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.25,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"RLI Corp Director Paul Bennett Medini Acquires 479.074 Shares Through Deferred Compensation Plan","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/rli-corp-director-paul-bennett-medini-acquires-479074-shares-through-deferred-compensation-plan","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793656522.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"RLI Corp Director Debbie Sharell Roberts Acquires 383.259 Shares Through Deferred Compensation Plan","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/rli-corp-director-debbie-sharell-roberts-acquires-383259-shares-through-deferred-compensation-plan","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793656520.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"RLI (RLI) Could Be 12% Undervalued Following Softer Third Quarter Earnings","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/insurance/nyse-rli/rli/news/rli-rli-could-be-12-undervalued-following-softer-third-quart","date":"2026-10-31","times